---
import Tag from '../components/Tag.astro';
import TerminalWindow from '../components/TerminalWindow.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const stack = ['typescript', 'react', 'java', 'spring-boot', 'kubernetes', 'jenkins'];
const interests = ['os-internals', 'security', 'assembly', 'hardware'];
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Fullstack developer at CHECK24, finishing a CS degree, endlessly curious about how computers actually work."
	pubDate={new Date('Aug 22 2026')}
>
	<TerminalWindow title="yasin@lowlevel:~/about">
		<p class="line"><span class="prompt">$</span> whoami</p>
		<p class="output">
			Fullstack developer at CHECK24, currently finishing my Computer Science bachelor's.
		</p>
	</TerminalWindow>

	<h2>work</h2>
	<p>
		At CHECK24 I own the application-management flow of the car insurance (KFZ) product end to
		end — frontend in TypeScript/React, backend in Java/Spring Boot. That includes the Jenkins
		pipelines that ship it and the Kubernetes setup it runs on.
	</p>
	<div class="tags">
		{stack.map((tag) => <Tag label={tag} />)}
	</div>

	<h2>off the clock</h2>
	<p>
		I like understanding things all the way down — how a CPU actually executes an instruction,
		how an OS schedules a process, how a system breaks when you push on it the wrong way. That
		curiosity is what this site is for: writing up what I dig into on the low-level and security
		side, outside of day-to-day web development.
	</p>
	<div class="tags">
		{interests.map((tag) => <Tag label={tag} />)}
	</div>

	<h2>elsewhere</h2>
	<p>
		Outside of code: breakdance and fitness. Different kind of practice, same instinct — take
		something apart, repeat it until it clicks, put it back together better.
	</p>
</Layout>

<style>
	.line {
		margin: 0 0 0.2em 0;
	}
	.prompt {
		color: var(--color-accent);
		margin-right: 0.5em;
	}
	.output {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}
	h2 {
		margin-top: 2em;
		font-size: 1.1em;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		text-transform: lowercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
	}
	.tags {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.4em;
		margin: -0.5em 0 1.5em 0;
	}
</style>
